# =============================================================
# .NET / ASP.NET Core Web API  ->  backend/
# =============================================================
bin/
obj/
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/

# The two rules above are for Visual Studio build output. They also matched
# android/app/src/debug/, which is not build output at all: it is the source
# folder Android uses for files that apply only to a debug build. Ours holds
# the network rule that lets a debug build reach the API over plain HTTP.
#
# Without these exceptions that file is never committed, and a member who
# clones the repository gets the release rule in their debug build. The app
# then fails with "CLEARTEXT communication to ... not permitted".
#
# The directory has to be un-ignored before its contents can be, because git
# does not look inside a directory it has already excluded.
!android/app/src/debug/
!android/app/src/debug/**

# Secrets: Mongo connection string, JWT signing key. NEVER commit.
# A committed *.example.json template shows the shape instead.
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.Production.json
appsettings.Local.json
secrets.json

# IIS publish output
publish/
*.pubxml.user

